13. Visual Flowcharts
====================================================================

**Overall Program Flow**

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Start: python dispute_processor.py] --> B{Load Modules & Globals}
    B --> C{Initialize Custom Embedding Function}
    C --> D{main() function starts}
    D --> E[Start Tee Logger]
    E --> F[Prompt User for Dispute ID]
    F --> G{Initialize ChromaDB Client}
    G --> H[Read Dispute Policies File]
    H --> I{Build & Populate ChromaDB Knowledge Base}
    I --> J{Initialize DisputeState (from dispute_db.json)}
    J --> K{If DisputeState Found}
    K -- Yes --> L[Print Initial State & Agents Sequentially (Demo)]
    L --> M{Call supervisor(DisputeState, Collection)}
    M --> N[Print Final DisputeState]
    N --> O[Stop Tee Logger]
    O --> P[End Program]
    K -- No --> P
```

**Supervisor Agent Orchestration Flow**

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[supervisor(state, collection) starts] --> B{Validate Initial Dispute Details (Pydantic)}
    B --> C{Initialize ThreadPoolExecutor}
    C --> D{Submit Agent 1: agent_get_transaction}
    C --> E{Submit Agent 2: agent_fraud_signal}
    C --> F{Submit Agent 3: Agent_merchant_details}
    D & E & F --> G{Wait for all Agents to complete (Future.result())}
    G --> H{Agents update 'state' object in parallel}
    H --> I{Validate Agent Data (Pydantic: transactionResponse, fraudResponse, merchantResponse)}
    I --> J{Update 'state' with validated data (model_dump())}
    J --> K{Retrieve key metrics from 'state' (fraud_score, dispute_rate, prev_dispute)}
    K --> L{Apply Decision Logic (if/elif/else)}
    L --> M{Update 'state.decision' and 'state.reason'}
    M --> N{Query ChromaDB (RAG) with dispute reason/amount}
    N --> O{Retrieve relevant policy context}
    O --> P{Update 'state.policy_context'}
    P --> Q[Return updated 'state' object]
```
